  1729	### 5.2 Session Event
  1730	
  1731	This subsection defines the immutable Session Event <code>1.0.0</code> base
  1732	variant used for post-creation changes under Session Record 1. It uses schema
  1733	<code>urn:ax:schema:session-event</code> version <code>1.0.0</code>. Sections
  1734	13.14.5 and 13.15 define the independently closed <code>2.0.0</code> and
  1735	<code>3.0.0</code> event variants; a reader MUST select the exact registered
  1736	major and MUST NOT interpret this base definition as their complete schema.
  1737	
  1738	Required fields are <code>event_id</code> digest, <code>subject_id</code> and
  1739	<code>session_id</code> with the same UUID,
  1740	<code>event_type</code>, <code>created_by_host_id</code>,
  1741	<code>lease_epoch</code>, <code>lease_id</code>, and
  1742	<code>lease_sequence</code> as a uint53 starting at 1 for
  1743	each lease,
  1744	<code>predecessors</code> as a sorted array of one or more record/event digests,
  1745	<code>created_at</code>, and <code>payload</code>. The first event after
  1746	creation MUST have exactly the Session Record ID in
  1747	<code>predecessors</code>; later events reference one or more prior event heads.
  1748	Events form a DAG; they are not ordered by timestamp.
  1749	The exact top-level shape also requires <code>schema</code>,
  1750	<code>schema_version</code>, and <code>extensions</code>; no other top-level
  1751	member is permitted.
  1752	
  1753	The winning owner MUST serialize state-changing events for a session. Within
  1754	one lease, <code>lease_sequence</code> MUST increase by exactly one and each
  1755	event MUST reference the immediately prior authoritative event. The first event
  1756	under a successor lease uses sequence 1 and references the predecessor
  1757	checkpoint's authoritative event heads. A missing sequence, two different
  1758	events at one sequence under the winning lease, or an event that omits the
  1759	required predecessor is <code>invalid_state_transition</code>; the session MUST
  1760	park and MUST NOT accept input until a newer explicit takeover establishes an
  1761	unambiguous checkpoint. Losing-lease branches remain preserved but are never
  1762	applied to authoritative state.
  1763	
  1764	The v1 event types are:
  1765	
  1766	<code>session.created</code>, <code>terminal.created</code>,
  1767	<code>provider.launched</code>, <code>provider.identified</code>,
  1768	<code>session.idle</code>, <code>session.quiescing</code>,
  1769	<code>checkpoint.created</code>, <code>sync.completed</code>,
  1770	<code>session.stopped</code>, <code>session.resumed</code>,
  1771	<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>,
  1772	<code>lease.transferred</code>, <code>lease.forced</code>,
  1773	<code>session.parked</code>, <code>session.failed</code>,
  1774	<code>fork.created</code>, <code>profile.changed</code>,
  1775	<code>session.tombstoned</code>, <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>,
  1776	<code>replica.replace_confirmed</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,
  1777	<code>task_board.adopted</code>, <code>tombstone.issued</code>, and
  1778	<code>tombstone.resolved</code>.
  1779	
  1780	The <code>payload</code> object is a closed tagged union selected by
  1781	<code>event_type</code>. It MUST contain exactly the members in this table; a
  1782	member shown as nullable remains required:
  1783	
