 11868	### 14.7 Session selector 1.0.0 and CLI Result 5.0.0
 11869	
 11870	This section is the v0.6.0 selector contract. It applies to the umbrella
 11871	<code>ax SELECTOR</code> and every existing managed-session NAME operand in
 11872	Section 14, including status, attach, takeover, fork, stop, resume, sync,
 11873	diff, materialize, logs --session and session set-profile. Creation NAME, destination HOST,
 11874	provider-native identifiers, Directory instance IDs/query expressions, and the
 11875	internal <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code> are not selector operands. No new
 11876	product operation or ownership authority is introduced.
 11877	
 11878	#### 14.7.1 Literal grammar and source-index resolution
 11879	
 11880	A selector is one CLI argument. Ordinary shell quoting handles spaces; the CLI
 11881	MUST NOT join multiple arguments, expand aliases as shell text, decode percent
 11882	escapes, normalize Unicode, trim, or case-fold configured host aliases. Split
 11883	at the FIRST literal <code>@</code> only. The key is either a Section 2 session
 11884	NAME or <code>id:SESSION_UUID</code>, with a canonical lowercase UUIDv7; neither
 11885	key form contains <code>@</code>. A bare UUID retains Section 2.3 name-first
 11886	precedence. <code>id:</code> explicitly bypasses names and never denotes a
 11887	provider-native ID, directory instance ID, lease ID, or UUID prefix.
 11888	
 11889	| Form | Meaning |
 11890	| --- | --- |
 11891	| <code>NAME</code> / bare UUID | Exact Section 2.3 local-name, peer-name, UUID, not-found precedence; collision refusal unchanged |
 11892	| <code>id:SESSION_UUID</code> | Durable AX session UUID in the local and allowed-peer union, independent of names |
 11893	| <code>KEY@local</code> | Only the local derived source index |
 11894	| <code>KEY@peer:ALIAS</code> | Only the configured peer source whose entire remaining suffix is the literal alias |
 11895	| <code>KEY@id:HOST_UUID</code> | Only the source whose canonical host UUID is given; local UUID selects local; otherwise exactly one allowlisted configured peer |
 11896	
 11897	Examples: <code>ax status build@local</code>,
 11898	<code>ax status build@peer:workstation</code>,
 11899	<code>ax status "build@peer:Work Laptop"</code>,
 11900	<code>ax status "build@peer:Ops@east:თბილისი"</code>, and
 11901	<code>ax status id:0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab</code>.
 11902	A percent sign in an alias is literal. <code>peer:</code> with an empty alias,
 11903	unknown source prefixes, malformed durable IDs, and an empty key are invalid
 11904	arguments. The alias obeys the existing configured name bound, 1–64 characters;
 11905	this grammar adds no alias encoding, normalization, or registration path.
 11906	
 11907	Resolution first validates configuration, including uniqueness of exact alias
 11908	and host-ID mappings. Duplicate source mappings are invalid_config, never
 11909	first-match selection. An explicit unknown alias/host is selector_source_not_found;
 11910	a known but disallowed peer is peer_not_allowlisted. A failed, partial, malformed,
 11911	or inaccessible config read is invalid_config. A remote source transport/I/O read failure is selector_source_read_failed
 11912	(exit 8); a local source/store I/O failure is the existing
 11913	local_precondition_failed (exit 3). A partial or malformed index/authority
 11914	response is integrity_failure (exit 9), not absence. A complete valid empty index
 11915	or a complete index without the selected live key returns not_found. A malformed
 11916	record or digest failure is integrity_failure. These outcomes MUST remain distinct.
 11917	An explicit source MUST NOT fall back to the local index, another peer, a cached
 11918	index from another source, or a union search, even when the same name/UUID exists
 11919	there. A peer source requires a complete read of that peer's advertised index
 11920	under the selected transport, with verified configured host identity; a local
 11921	cached observation does not prove that read succeeded.
 11922	
 11923	For a qualified NAME, select in that source only: exact live name first, then
 11924	exact UUID if the NAME is UUID-shaped. Deduplicate multiple copies of the same
 11925	session UUID only when their immutable record digest agrees. Distinct live
 11926	UUIDs with the same name or ASCII-fold-colliding names return name_ambiguous.
 11927	For bare input retain exactly Section 2.3 tiers: a local exact match wins over a
 11928	peer exact match; a peer exact match wins over UUID interpretation. Collision
 11929	checks apply within the reached tier. Unread lower tiers need not be consulted
 11930	after a unique higher-tier match. A tier that must be read but cannot be read
 11931	is a read failure, not permission to proceed to a lower tier. Tombstoned entries
 11932	are excluded only with authoritative tombstone evidence, not a failed record read.
 11933	
