  8245	#### 11.10.4 Assurance and executable fixture bounds
  8246	
  8247	TLS proves possession of an enrolled private key and protects records. It does
  8248	not prove unique physical hardware, current ownership of a Session, or an
  8249	uncompromised operator/account. A copied key authenticates until each verifier
  8250	revokes it. An attacker able to read/replace local AX state, credentials or
  8251	binaries is outside this assurance. Arbitrary shell access to that account
  8252	cannot be made safe by a wrapper. A restricted server-enforced SSH account is
  8253	an alternative deployment hardening measure, not equivalent host evidence and
  8254	not a substitute for this profile. Remote attach/log CLI paths remain their
  8255	existing SSH contracts; they do not acquire RPC-5 host-channel assurance.
  8256	
  8257	The following closed gate registry defines source-level fixture families.
  8258	Each family MUST have positive and negative vectors. These are contract model
  8259	checks, not an executed TLS deployment, private-key custody proof or product
  8260	conformance result. Real certificate-chain, handshake, race/timeout and platform
  8261	acceptance remains required by <code>AC-HOST-001</code>.
  8262	
  8263	| Gate | Predicate required for admission |
  8264	| --- | --- |
  8265	| HC-TLS | Both peers verify full TLS 1.3 and exact ALPN; no resumption or early data |
  8266	| HC-CERT | Standard chain, profile, time and role verification succeed in both directions |
  8267	| HC-MAP | Exact enrolled leaf/root/key maps uniquely to the configured UUID |
  8268	| HC-HELLO | Both hello IDs equal verified UUIDs and nonce/contract/limit validation succeeds |
  8269	| HC-DISPATCH | No application dispatch before mutual TLS and hello success |
  8270	| HC-MIGRATE | Config 4 selects the explicit Host Channel 1 launch and RPC 5 only |
  8271	| HC-LIFECYCLE | Explicit enrollment and bounded fresh-key rotation; revoked keys never reenter |
  8272	| HC-GENERATION | Dispatch and every mutation boundary use the current committed authorization generation |
  8273	| HC-EXCLUDE | Credential and trust material remains local, outside replication |
  8274	| HC-PARITY | The same TLS requirements apply over OpenSSH and native Tailscale SSH |
  8275	
  8276	#### 11.10.5 Executable admission obligations
  8277	
  8278	The following closed JSON policy is normative source for the synthetic admission
  8279	predicates. The public validator reads it from SPEC.md on every invocation;
  8280	there is no independently hard-coded admission model. Every field is required,
  8281	unknown fields refuse, and all field predicates must hold. Predicates apply to
  8282	every invocation, including request, resume, retry, queue and recovery, on both
  8283	SSH transports; client/server facts are separate required obligations. The entrypoint and
  8284	carrier facts are synthetic execution context, not new RPC wire members. A
  8285	conditional predicate cannot grant an exception to another obligation.
  8286	
  8287	Operators are closed: `eq` is type-exact JSON equality; `range` is an inclusive
  8288	integer interval (booleans excluded); `in` is type-exact set membership;
  8289	`equal_field` is type-exact equality with another present field; `singleton_field`
  8290	is exactly a one-element array of that field; `uuid7` requires the canonical
  8291	lowercase UUIDv7 grammar; `all` is conjunction. `when` has exactly `field`, `in`
  8292	and `require`: it applies its predicate only when the named fact is in the given
  8293	set. It exists to make scope changes executable and testable, not to authorize
  8294	narrowing the universal obligations in this revision. Missing or mistyped
  8295	operands, duplicate keys, unsupported operators and unreadable policy refuse.
  8296	
  8297	The table following the JSON is rendered from these predicates. The detailed
  8298	Section 6.6 and 11.10.1–4 explanations are checked against the review-bound
  8299	renderer templates in `scripts/host_channel_templates/`; they cannot be changed
  8300	by refreshing the five-document prose digest. Templates are implementation
  8301	inputs, not another normative specification. Changes to a predicate must pass
  8302	independent vectors even when the table has been regenerated. Changes to the
  8303	explanation require reviewing its renderer too. Projection agreement is an
  8304	integrity check, **not** natural-language semantic proof.
  8305	
  8306	Coverage counts individually witnessed executable field obligations from this
  8307	policy, separately from family coverage and explanation projection. A witness
  8308	must show admission with the obligation satisfied and refusal caused by that
  8309	obligation alone on a well-shaped vector. Missing-field controls prove the
  8310	closed schema separately. Detailed DER parsing, issuance, filesystem custody,
  8311	transaction crash durability and live TLS/SSH scheduling are not discharged by
  8312	boolean facts; their behavioral coverage is unknown, as is semantic coverage of
  8313	unstructured prose outside these projections. Product acceptance still requires
  8314	AC-HOST-001. No coverage ratio here measures those runtime requirements.
