  9153	The task-board launch remains in the same bootstrap window until step 7. The
  9154	direct bootstrap rules apply with bridge status and caller-stable launch/export
  9155	IDs replacing PID/native-store reconciliation:
  9156	
  9157	| Fixture/boundary | Required recovery |
  9158	| --- | --- |
  9159	| <code>BOOT-TB-BEFORE-LAUNCH</code> | Resume retries the same launch operation/body; no manager may exist under a new operation ID |
  9160	| <code>BOOT-TB-AFTER-LAUNCH</code> | Reconcile the public manager reference and exact Ax Binding, then retry export; do not inspect private state |
  9161	| <code>BOOT-TB-AFTER-EXPORT</code> | Reconcile the same export operation, validate bundle/proof, and publish the first checkpoint |
  9162	| <code>BOOT-TB-ABORT</code> | Bridge force-stop closes or proves absent the exact manager; emit bootstrap abort with null checkpoint and non-resumable failed state |
  9163	
  9164	An ambiguous manager binding or status prevents both a second launch and a
