  9167	
  9168	### 13.3 Sync
  9169	
  9170	Preconditions:
  9171	
  9172	- source and destination are allowlisted and complete the RPC handshake;
  9173	- relevant contract major versions are compatible; and
  9174	- any owner-authored checkpoint carries the current winning lease.
  9175	
  9176	Sync normally transfers the newest already validated checkpoint and does not
  9177	pause a running provider. If the owner elects to create a fresh checkpoint, it
  9178	MUST first establish the Section 7.6 safe boundary; a task-board session uses
  9179	bridge <code>export --mode snapshot</code> so input is released before sync
  9180	continues. A replica MUST never ask a provider or manager to create a new
  9181	checkpoint.
  9182	
  9183	Transitions:
  9184	
  9185	1. Exchange lease heads and inventory Merkle roots.
  9186	2. Union missing immutable records/events/tombstones and derive the winning
  9187	   lease.
  9188	3. Identify referenced manifests/blobs absent from either peer.
  9189	4. Begin or resume staged chunk transfer.
  9190	5. Validate and atomically commit immutable objects.
  9191	6. Optionally call <code>materialize.prepare</code> with
  9192	   <code>intent = passive_replica</code>, the selected checkpoint sessions in
  9193	   <code>materialization_session_ids</code>, and an empty ownership-transfer
  9194	   set. Choose workspace/composite when workspace bytes participate and
  9195	   provider/task-board only when they do not. A stopped replica is valid. The
  9196	   destination may commit/finalize only as dormant and MUST NOT run or resume a
  9197	   provider.
  9198	7. Record a <code>sync.completed</code> observation with counts/digests, never
  9199	   payload contents.
  9200	
  9201	Syncing a replica MUST NOT run or resume the provider. A conflict MAY leave
  9202	immutable objects synchronized while workspace materialization remains
  9203	blocked; the result is partial and MUST use exit 15. A transport failure leaves
  9204	verified staging resumable.
  9205	
  9206	The <code>--all</code> selector widens only which eligible immutable namespaces
  9207	and policy-allowed projections are converged. ax sync --all MUST NOT change
  9208	ownership or launch a runtime. It MUST NOT select takeover, adopt, resume,
  9209	provider launch, task-board open/adopt, or another mutating continuation as an
  9210	implicit consequence of synchronization.
  9211	
  9212	### 13.4 Local attach
  9213	
  9214	<code>ax attach NAME --local</code> requires the local host to be the winning
  9215	owner and the wrapper to be attachable. Before connecting input, it MUST refresh
  9216	the lease from reachable peers or state that it is operating on the latest
  9217	known lease within the configured refresh interval.
  9218	
  9219	If a higher or winning same-epoch lease is observed, the wrapper MUST block
  9220	input, park or terminate its stale provider according to policy, preserve
  9221	diagnostics, and return <code>stale_owner</code>. Attach never changes
  9222	ownership.
  9223	
  9224	### 13.5 Remote attach
  9225	
  9226	Remote attach targets the current winning owner and never creates a destination
  9227	runtime, changes a lease, or converts itself into takeover. A stale destination
  9228	hint is re-resolved to the current owner or fails; it is not authority to attach
  9229	to a replica.
  9230	
  9231	Preconditions:
  9232	
  9233	- a remote allowlisted host is the winning owner;
  9234	- SSH authentication succeeds; and
  9235	- the remote wrapper is attachable.
  9236	
  9237	The local process executes the argv-equivalent of:
  9238	
  9239	~~~shell
  9240	ssh -t HOST ax attach NAME --local
  9241	~~~
  9242	
  9243	The remote command resolves NAME again and verifies the lease before accepting
  9244	input. The initiating host remains a replica. No Lease Record, workspace
  9245	materialization, provider snapshot, or task-board adoption is changed.
  9246	
  9247	If SSH disconnects, the provider and durable terminal continue on the owner.
  9248	The operator MAY run remote attach again. If the owner cannot be reached, the
  9249	command reports <code>owner_unreachable</code> and suggests graceful takeover
  9250	only when contact returns, explicit force takeover, fork from the newest local
  9251	checkpoint, or cancel.
  9252	
  9253	### 13.6 Graceful takeover
  9254	
  9255	Command form is <code>ax takeover NAME --to HOST</code>; <code>--to</code>
  9256	defaults to the local host in interactive use.
  9257	
  9258	Preconditions:
  9259	
  9260	- source is reachable and proves it holds the winning lease;
  9261	- destination is allowlisted, is not the source, and has compatible contracts;
  9262	- destination provider/platform capabilities required by the session are
  9263	  available;
  9264	- on macOS, the destination Aqua broker, dedicated AX tmux server generation,
