   436	
   437	## Provider Plugin JSONL Protocol
   438	
   439	[`internal/provhost`](internal/provhost) implements the ax host side of
   440	the Section 7.2 provider plugin JSON-over-stdio protocol: one-frame JSONL
   441	transport, deadlines, size limits, stdout/stderr separation, operation
   442	dispatch, and status recovery. `Host.Call` is the production entry point.
   443	It frames one request envelope (`protocol`, `protocol_version`,
   444	`request_id`, `operation`, `deadline`, `body`), starts one plugin process
   445	per operation, enforces the request deadline, and interprets the single
   446	response frame. Unknown operations, stale deadlines, and unframeable
   447	bodies are refused with `invalid_config` before any process starts.
   448	
   449	Each stdout line must be one complete UTF-8 JSON object no larger than 8
   450	MiB; stdout carries the single response frame while diagnostics stay on
   451	stderr and never enter failure text. A recognizable foreign major yields
   452	`incompatible_protocol` without trusting the payload; every other
   453	unusable frame yields `provider_protocol_error`, both as local Structured
   454	Error 1.0.0 objects built without adopting any child-supplied code,
   455	retryable bit, details, or authority. A plugin that exceeds its deadline
   456	is terminated (as a process group on unix; direct-child kill on Windows)
   457	and reported as `provider_timeout`; a
   458	crash without a response is `provider_process_failed`. On success the raw
   459	body is returned for the operation layer; on failure the bound child
   460	error is returned itself. All six codes are pinned against the contract
   461	registry with their exact exits (3, 13, 6, 13, 13, 9).
   462	
   463	Dispatch covers exactly the 15 Section 7.5 operations in manifest order,
   464	derived from the pinned specification text, and refuses any other name
   465	without spawning. Status recovery interprets `materialize-status` bodies
   466	through the Section 7.5 state rules: unknown fails closed with
   467	`integrity_failure` for quarantine, prepared requires plan, token, and
   468	discovery, terminal states require plan and discovery with no token, and
   469	identity members must equal the requested transaction. Reads evolve —
   470	prepared under one envelope may be committed under the next — and each
   471	call starts a fresh process, so recovery observes durable state through
   472	the passed authority with no host-side mutation cache.
   473	
   474	The operation layer validates what a plugin returned: the closed
   475	Section 7.3 manifest (registries derived from the pinned example),
   476	the Section 7.4 probe with its seven capability values (only
   477	`available` may be `enabled`), the host-side capability gate
   478	(`RequireCapability` refuses unproven surfaces before any process
