  1833	## Session selector, read summaries, and selection plans
  1834	
  1835	`internal/sessquery` is the single shared selector API over the persisted
  1836	session repositories and the accepted state projector. It implements the
  1837	v0.6.0 selector contract (§14.7/§14.7.1, refining §2.3) with shared
  1838	SelectionPlan construction and revalidation (§14.7.2):
  1839	
  1840	- Literal grammar: split at the first `@` only. The key is a NAME, a bare
  1841	  UUID (name-first precedence kept), or `id:UUID` (bypasses names for the
  1842	  durable union identity). The source is empty (bare §2.3 tiers), `local`,
  1843	  `peer:ALIAS` (the entire remaining suffix, literal — spaces, `@`,
  1844	  Unicode, and `%` included), or `id:HOST_UUID`. No joining, aliasing,
  1845	  percent-decoding, Unicode normalization, trimming, or alias folding.
  1846	- Exact source mappings: effective configuration (local host, peer
  1847	  alias/host mappings, allowlist) is validated first, including exact
  1848	  alias and host-ID uniqueness; duplicates are `invalid_config`.
  1849	  Explicit unknown aliases/hosts are `selector_source_not_found`; known
  1850	  but disallowed peers are `peer_not_allowlisted`. Remote read failures
  1851	  are `selector_source_read_failed` with the cause preserved; local I/O
  1852	  keeps its repository error; malformed authority is `integrity_failure`.
  1853	- No explicit-source fallback: a qualified key resolves in its one
  1854	  source only. Tier, collision, and tombstone semantics follow §14.7.1:
  1855	  exact live name then UUID-shaped name within the source, replicated
  1856	  copies deduplicate only on agreeing record digests (else
  1857	  `integrity_failure`), distinct colliding names refuse with
  1858	  `name_ambiguous`, and tombstoned entries stay excluded on
  1859	  authoritative tombstone evidence while failed reads never count as it.
  1860	- Immutable plans: `Reader.BuildPlan` binds all sixteen §14.7.2
  1861	  members — the literal selector, session and validated record digest,
  1862	  source host (always a UUIDv7; a local selection without a known local
  1863	  host refuses `invalid_config`) and exact alias, index and
