  1906	chains through `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the
  1907	derived identity, provider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role,
  1908	checkpoint ID, conflicts, and warnings as an internal `Summary`. List
  1909	order is bytewise session ID; `InspectLocal` retains raw access to
  1910	parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics and is not a public
  1911	summary entry. Failed index reads and failed projections propagate as
  1912	errors. Repository-parked sessions remain visible in listing but are
  1913	excluded from live routing. Reading never repairs a store or performs
  1914	an attach, resume, or ownership change. Creating is a record AND an
  1915	authoritative initial lease (§5.7/§13.1 step 2), so a record-only chain
  1916	is an interrupted prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf: list and
  1917	status refuse it with `selector_bootstrap_incomplete` — the whole list
  1918	when any encountered record is unrepresentable — instead of returning
  1919	an ownerless row or a placeholder owner. The closed authoritative
  1920	layer (`Reader.AuthoritativeStatus`, `Reader.AuthoritativeList`)
  1921	binds owner, lease, and role from the validated winning Lease Record,
  1922	owner display names only from validated host metadata (1..64), local
  1923	roles only with a known local host, checkpoint timestamps only from
  1924	validated observations, workspace_status from the closed five-value
  1925	enum, capabilities from validated CapabilitySummary maps (0..7, only
  1926	available may enable) keyed by exactly the provhost-owned Section 7.3
  1927	seven-name provider registry (any other name refuses
  1928	`invalid_config`), process liveness as a required boolean for
  1929	status, and warnings from the projection; unknown required
  1930	observations refuse `selector_observation_unavailable` while
  1931	established absence (workspace absent, empty non-nil capabilities)
  1932	stays representable, and nothing is inferred.
  1933	
  1934	These entries do not provide an `ax` executable or a closed CLI Result
  1935	renderer. CLI Result 5 with Structured Error 1.4.0, wire exit binding,
  1936	transports, peer authentication, and lifecycle effects belong to their
  1937	owning leaves.
  1938	`TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult` drives the refused
  1939	`Reader.List`/`Reader.Status` entries and the existing `cliresult.New`
  1940	to demonstrate that a creating session without owner facts satisfies
  1941	neither the summary entries nor the mandatory CLI owner/lease fields.
  1942	No owner is invented and no doctor/provider/platform capability
  1943	is advertised. The traceability, gate battery, and remaining bounds are
  1944	in [the task evidence map](internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md).
  1945	
  1946	```bash
  1947	go test ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo -count=1 -v
  1948	python3 internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py /absolute/path/to/new/evidence-dir
  1030	// never consulted and branching history stays admissible. A
  1031	// missing, wrong-session, wrong-lease, wrong-creator,
