--- /dev/null
+++ b//Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/relation-census-rev12.md
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+# TASK-260830-21gygk rev12 relation census
+
+Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec v0.6.0, commit
+`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`, with the retained v0.5.0
+relationships. This census records the owned 5.3/5.4 relationships that
+were rechecked for CR11 temporal authority. It is evidence for the shared
+library boundary; CLI publication, transport, fencing, and durable summary
+storage remain caller-owned bounds.
+
+## K4 temporal and checkpoint relationships
+
+| ID | Required relationship | Production owner and inputs | Positive controls | Negative/refusal controls |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| K4-1 | The referenced checkpoint owner is the consuming resume's lease or an earlier lease in the same winning succession. | `internal/sessquery/lease.go:938-951` locates the owner in the admitted winner-to-root `[]validatedLease`; `admitCheckpoint` at `:579-610` calls `checkReferencedCheckpointTemporal`; `:959-1008` compares the owner and resume positions through `leaseChainIndex` and refuses `ErrObservationUnavailable` when the owner is later. | `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority` good, good_prechange, and good_divergent; `TestRev12ReferencedCheckpointLaterLease` proves a later-lease resume may consume an earlier checkpoint. | `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority` future_owner and epoch_mismatch cases run direct and task_board, winner and ancestor, through BuildPlan, fresh/old-plan Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus, and AuthoritativeList. The future-owner cases fail with `selector_observation_unavailable`. |
+| K4-2 | Every checkpoint event head is an authoritative chained event for the same session at or before the owning lease; historical heads remain admissible. | `checkCheckpointEventHeads` at `internal/sessquery/lease.go:641-666` reads `Repository.ListEvents`, resolves each head, and checks epoch and fencing token against the owner. `admitCheckpoint` calls it before profile derivation. | `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority` control cases, `TestValidSuccessorBuildsAndRevalidates`, `TestEpochOneWithSelfBoundCheckpointBuilds`, and the `good_prechange`/historical controls in `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority`. | `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority` missing_head and later_lease_head cases, each winner/ancestor and each shared entry plus old-plan Revalidate, refuse `ErrObservationUnavailable`. `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority` also pins the refusal class before profile derivation. |
+| K4-3 | A consuming resume must descend from every event head named by its referenced checkpoint. | `checkReferencedCheckpointTemporal` at `:971-1007` builds the authoritative event map from `ListEvents`, walks the resume's predecessor closure, treats the repository-validated Session Record digest as the genesis boundary, and rejects a head outside that closure. | Same-lease and historical `good`/`good_prechange` controls in `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority`; `TestRev12ReferencedCheckpointLaterLease` covers a later consuming lease with the earlier head in its predecessor path. | `future_owner`, `epoch_mismatch`, and the old-plan narrowing path in `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority`; unknown or later heads remain covered by `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority` and referenced `bad_unknown_head` controls. |
+| K4-4 | Each necessary ancestry checkpoint is for the session and predecessor lease, created by that lease holder, and uses the Session.kind-selected persistence variant. | `checkCheckpointBinding` at `internal/sessquery/lease.go:557-572` and the shared `admitCheckpoint` owner at `:579-610` apply session, lease tuple, creator-holder, persistence, event-head, and profile checks to winner and ancestor checkpoints. | `TestRev5AncestorCheckpointAuthority`, `TestRev5CheckpointCreatorMustBeHolder`, `TestRev6CheckpointPersistenceMustMatchSession`, and their direct/task_board controls. | Missing/wrong ancestor checkpoint, wrong creator, and wrong variant cases in the same tests refuse through all shared entries and old-plan Revalidate. |
+
+## Authority and caller boundary
+
+The raw `validatedCheckpoint` shape is confined to parsing and the explicit
+admission owners. `admittedCheckpoint` is constructed only by
+`admitCheckpoint`; profile derivation functions accept that capability, and
+`buildCheckpointAdmission` is the only capability supplied to referenced
+profile derivation. `TestRev11RecordConsumptionCensus` and
+`TestRev12RecordConsumptionCensusRejectsAlternatePaths` exercise the
+package-wide go/types boundary, including raw maps and values in a new file,
+method receiver, closure factory, and inferred loader result.
+
+The shared API owns plan construction, revalidation, and the authoritative
+summary value/refusal decisions. `Reader.List`, `Reader.Status`,
+`Reader.AuthoritativeStatus`, and `Reader.AuthoritativeList` do not publish a
+CLI Result, persist a plan, perform fencing, or transport a remote action.
+Those caller-owned responsibilities are stated bounds, not unsupported
+capabilities.
+
+## Acceptance ratio
+
+The shared library owns **8 of 8 AC rows**: selector resolution and
+ambiguity, source/error mapping, immutable SelectionPlan construction and
+revalidation, checkpoint/lease authority, authoritative list/status
+summaries, deterministic sorting, and negative/recovery evidence. The CLI
+surface owns **0 of 8 rows** in this deliverable: no `ax` executable, wire
+Result renderer, transport, fencing, or publication capability is advertised.
