+# TASK-260830-21gygk: v0.6.0 clause-to-owner conformance matrix
+
+Candidate source: `e119aaeede327580a470238fdb1ccf340a785b39` plus the
+uncommitted task candidate in the managed Story worktree. Authority is
+`agent-session-manager-spec` v0.6.0 at
+`0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`; retained compatibility scope is
+v0.5.0 at `28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`.
+
+This matrix records the implemented shared-library boundary. It does not
+claim that the `ax` CLI or lifecycle leaves have been implemented in this
+task. Those callers own invoking the shared API at their required boundaries.
+
+| Normative clause / fact | Owning production entry and implementation | Evidence through the production entry | Bound or explicit non-owner |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| 14.7.1 literal selector grammar | `Reader.Resolve` -> `ParseSelector`; `resolveBare` and `resolveExplicit` | `TestParseSelectorLiteralGrammar`, `TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceRefusals` | First literal `@`, exact `local`/`peer:`/`id:` forms, and exact aliases are library behavior; CLI wire exit binding remains with the CLI leaf. |
+| 2.3 bare tier precedence | `Reader.Resolve` -> `resolveBare` -> `liveCandidates`/`selectIdentity` | `TestPinnedPrecedence`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion`, `TestResolveAllowlistAndReadFailures` | Local exact live name, allowlisted peer exact live name, then UUID union; parked and tombstoned entries are excluded from live selection. |
+| Qualified source and no fallback | `resolveExplicit` -> `locateSource` -> one source read and source-local selection | `TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack`, `TestResolveQualifiedNameBeforeUUIDInSource`, `TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures` | A valid explicit source is never replaced by a lower tier or another source; absent source and read failure retain distinct errors. |
+| Ambiguity and replicated identity | `matchName`, `selectIdentity`, `checkRecordAgreement` | `TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions`, `TestResolveQualifiedAmbiguityAndExclusions`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` | ASCII-fold collisions refuse; agreeing replicated records deduplicate deterministically; contradictory record digests refuse integrity. |
+| Stable deterministic ordering | `Reader.read`, `peerCandidates`, `selectIdentity` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity`, `TestResolveBareIdentityUnion` | Session IDs and peer source IDs use bytewise order; identical-copy ties use bytewise holder-host order. |
+| 5.3 winning lease and succession | `Reader.winningLeaseFor` -> `checkLeaseChain` | `TestValidSuccessorBuildsAndRevalidates`, `TestSuccessorCycleMustRefuse`, `TestSkippedEpochMustRefuse`, `TestDanglingPredecessorMustRefuse`, `TestBuildWithLaggingLeaseCopy` | Greatest `(epoch, lease_id)` winner is selected from canonical Lease Records; predecessor ancestry is complete and lagging copies remain non-authoritative history. |
+| 5.4 checkpoint semantic admission | `checkWinnerCheckpoint`, `checkCheckpointBinding` -> shared `admitCheckpoint` | `TestRev5AncestorCheckpointAuthority`, `TestRev5CheckpointCreatorMustBeHolder`, `TestRev5AncestorCheckpointBinding`, `TestRev6CheckpointPersistenceMustMatchSession`, `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority` | Every necessary checkpoint is admitted for session, owning lease tuple, creator-holder, persistence variant, and event-head closure. Raw parsed checkpoints do not authorize profile derivation. |
+| 5.3/5.4 temporal authority | `checkReferencedCheckpointBinding` -> `checkReferencedCheckpointTemporal` -> `admitCheckpoint` | `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority`, `TestRev12ReferencedCheckpointLaterLease` | A referenced checkpoint owner must be at or before the consuming resume lease; its event heads must be in the resume predecessor closure. A later consumer may use an earlier checkpoint. Same-lease and historical controls remain valid. |
+| 2.4 profile authority | `checkCheckpointProfileAuthority` and profile derivation helpers | `TestRev8ProfileHistoricalClosureAdmits`, `TestRev8ProfileOldPlanSubstitution`, `TestReview9ResumeReferencedCheckpoint`, `TestRev10ResumeReferencedCheckpoint`, `TestReview10ReferencedCheckpointAdmission` | Profile derivation accepts only `admittedCheckpoint`; missing/wrong session, lease, creator, variant, future-owned, or unresolved-head references refuse `selector_observation_unavailable`; contradictory profile pairs refuse integrity. |
+| Type-level raw-record boundary | package-wide `go/types` census in `rev11_regression_test.go`; production owner is `admitCheckpoint` plus loader/binding helpers | `TestRev11RecordConsumptionCensus`, `TestRev12RecordConsumptionCensusRejectsAlternatePaths`, `TestRev12AdmissionPrecisionCensus` | New files, methods, closures, inferred maps, and alternate raw checkpoint paths are rejected by the same census. The AST census is precision evidence only; semantic temporal tests provide behavioral coverage. |
+| 14.7.2 BuildPlan | `Reader.BuildPlan` -> `bindPlan` -> `winningLeaseFor` and shared checkpoint admission | `TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts`, `TestBuildPlanValidatesUnionAtBuild`, `TestRev5AncestorCheckpointAuthority`, `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority`, `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority` | Selection is resolved once; the immutable plan binds selector, UUID, record, source/config/index, canonical Lease Record digest and tuple, authority heads, action, destination, and expectations. |
+| 14.7.2 Revalidate | `Reader.Revalidate` -> `validateAuthorityUnion` and `collectAuthorityHeads` | `TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange`, `TestRevalidateUnionLeaseDivergenceRefusesStale`, `TestRevalidateUnionTombstoneRefusesStale`, `TestRevalidateUnionParkedCopyRefuses`, `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority` | Current facts are reread and compared; no name re-resolution, substitution, silent replan, lease transfer, or reused confirmation. Old-plan temporal cases are exercised through the same entry. |
+| Authority union and heads | `validateAuthorityUnion`, `collectAuthorityHeads` | `TestBuildPlanValidatesUnionAtBuild`, `TestReviewerOtherSourceDivergenceMustRefuse`, `TestBuildWithLaggingLeaseCopy`, `TestRevalidateUnionUnreadablePeerRefuses` | Allowed-source record/lease/tombstone contradictions and required parked/unreadable copies refuse; agreeing and lagging copies remain current. Heads are sorted unique tails plus the winning Lease Record digest. |
+| 5.7 internal list/status projection | `Reader.List`, `Reader.Status` -> `Repository.ListSessions`/`Resolve` -> `Projector.Project` | `TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder`, `TestListStatusCheckpointAndProjectionFailure`, `TestCreatingSummaryCannotClaimClosedCLIResult`, `TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole` | Lists/statuses expose only verified projection facts and refuse record-only completed reads as `selector_bootstrap_incomplete`; read paths do not mutate durable state. |
+| 5.7/14.7.3 authoritative summaries | `Reader.AuthoritativeStatus`, `Reader.AuthoritativeList` -> `authorize` | `TestAuthoritativeStatusHealthy`, `TestAuthoritativeMissingHostMetadataRefuses`, `TestAuthoritativeUnknownObservationsRefuse`, `TestAuthoritativeInputValidation`, `TestAuthoritativeAdmitsFullCapabilityRegistry`, `TestReview11ReferencedTemporalAuthority` | Owner/lease/host/workspace/capability/process/checkpoint observations are validated or refused; no proxy facts are inferred. The shared leaf does not publish CLI wire documents or own caller-side storage/transport. |
+| 14.7.4 recovery and durable effects | Caller/lifecycle owner | `TestParkedReadRecoveryAndMissingVsMalformed` covers read-after-interrupted-create composition | This task performs no recovery effect, attach, fencing, commit, retry, dispatch, transport, or publication. `InspectLocal` is an explicit internal diagnostic read, not a public summary substitute. |
+| Capability vocabulary | `authorize` via the provhost-owned seven-name registry | `TestAuthoritativeAdmitsFullCapabilityRegistry`, `TestRev4UnknownCapabilityMustRefuse` | Exactly the seven supported capability names are admitted; no new capability is advertised by this task. |
